  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The solid is a **pentagonal pyramid** since it is a pyramid whose base is a pentagon.\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a triangular pyramid since not all its faces are triangular.\n\n- The solid is not a pentagonal prism since it has only one pentagonal face.\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles. Due to the same reasons, the solid is not a cube.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-61656\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>The solid is a <strong>pentagonal pyramid</strong> since it is a pyramid whose base is a pentagon.</p>\n<p>Also, notice that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The solid is not a triangular pyramid since not all its faces are triangular.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The solid is not a pentagonal prism since it has only one pentagonal face.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles. Due to the same reasons, the solid is not a cube. </p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
